guide = heading('GETTING STARTED','From first launch<br>to <span class="pink">first download.</span>','A short guide to getting comfortable with AIM Downloader.') + '''<div class="wrap guide-layout"><aside class="guide-index"><p class="eyebrow">IN THIS GUIDE</p><a href="#install">01 · Install or extract</a><a href="#setup">02 · Complete setup</a><a href="#link">03 · Add your links</a><a href="#formats">04 · Choose your format</a><a href="#queue">05 · Manage your queue</a><a href="#files">06 · Find your files</a></aside><div class="guide-content">
<section id="install"><span class="step-label">01 / GET THE APP</span><h2>Install. Or just extract.</h2><p>Download the Windows installer and follow its prompts. It installs for your account and can add a desktop shortcut.</p><p>Prefer the portable edition? Extract the complete ZIP into a writable folder, then open <code>AIM-DOWNLOADER.exe</code>. Keep the extracted files together.</p><a href="/download/" class="text-link">Choose your download →</a></section>
<section id="setup"><span class="step-label">02 / FIRST LAUNCH</span><h2>Give AIM a place to work.</h2><p>Follow the welcome steps, choose your download folder, and let automatic tool setup complete. AIM downloads and verifies the tools it needs for supported media.</p><p>Keep your internet connection active. If setup is interrupted, use Retry. You do not need to install Python or .NET separately.</p></section>
<section id="link"><span class="step-label">03 / ADD YOUR MEDIA</span><h2>It starts with a link.</h2><p>Choose your quality preset and duplicate policy first. Turn Auto-Download off if you want to review items before they start. Then paste a public video or playlist URL and add it to AIM. With Auto-Download off, playlists open a selection window so you can choose the entries to keep.</p><p>With Auto-Download on, added links start immediately and playlist entries are queued automatically. You can also import a text file of URLs. Private, account-only, and cookie-dependent media are outside the supported workflow.</p></section>
<section id="formats"><span class="step-label">04 / MAKE IT YOURS</span><h2>Choose video or audio.</h2><p>Choose the available quality and format before queueing. Source media determines which options are available.</p><ul><li><strong>Best video:</strong> preserves the original codecs and merges video and audio without re-encoding video.</li><li><strong>MP4 compatible:</strong> uses compatible H.264/AAC formats when the source offers them.</li><li><strong>Original audio:</strong> extracts the source audio.</li><li><strong>MP3:</strong> converts the audio to MP3.</li></ul><p>Choose a preset before adding links. Available results depend on the source; selecting a higher quality cannot create a format the source does not offer.</p></section>
<section id="queue"><span class="step-label">05 / FOLLOW THE PROGRESS</span><h2>Keep your queue moving.</h2><p>Add selected items to the queue. AIM uses three simultaneous download slots by default; you can adjust concurrency in Settings. Use Pause and Resume / Retry as needed; some sources may restart transfers.</p><p>Pause is unavailable while files are merging or converting. Cancel stops the current job and removes its temporary staging files.</p><p>For duplicate files, choose Skip, Keep both, or Replace based on what you want to keep.</p></section>
<section id="files"><span class="step-label">06 / ENJOY THE RESULT</span><h2>Right where you left them.</h2><p>Open a completed file or its output folder from the queue. Your chosen download folder contains the finished media.</p><p>Removing a queue record does not delete its completed file. Keep enough free disk space for both your downloads and temporary processing.</p><div class="notice">Only download media you have permission to save.</div></section></div></div>'''

